{
  "abstract": "Late-stage model growth—keeping a language model narrow and shallow for 50%–75% of pretraining tokens before expanding to target capacity—saves 22%–34% of FLOPs, but existing operators degrade during linear learning-rate cooldown. Under Muon+AdamW, zero-readout insertion ($G_{\\text{zero}}$) avoids forward shock (`0.000000` nats) but blocks step-1 backward gradients into internal projections ($+0.0188$ to $+0.0231$ validation bits-per-byte, BPB), whereas stacked expansion ($G_{\\text{stack}} + \\text{SPARKLING}$) incurs a $+0.23\\text{--}1.12$ nat shock and preconditions differential width gradients through a shared Gram matrix with quintic gain $q_5(s_j^2)=f_5(s_j)/s_j$ without an aspect-ratio LR boost on wide readouts $W_{\\text{proj}} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d\\times 2d_{\\text{ff}}}$ (Theorem 1B). We introduce Hadamard Modal-Decoupled Late Morphogenesis (`HSDM-2D`): (1) Whole-Block Dual Straight-Through Residual Homotopy (`DSTRH`, Theorem 3); (2) Stiefel (`stiefel_tangent`) or zero-loss Isometric Polar-Express (`isometric_pe`) splitting with $2\\times 2$ (`H_2`) and $4\\times 4$ Kronecker Hadamard (`H_2 \\otimes H_2`) Modal Muon (`modal_hadamard`, Theorems 2A–2B); and (3) Stage-2 micro-batch subdivision (`accum 4->2`). Across 222 runs, 3-seed fixed-batch `HSDM-2D` at 65.9% tokens (`accum=4`) beats default-schedule $G_{\\text{stack}} + \\text{SPARKLING Eq. 28}$ under `stiefel_tangent` ($p = 0.00180$), `isometric_pe + cos2` ($p = 0.00214$), and `isometric_pe + dual_clock` ($p = 0.00156$), and at 75.1% tokens (`accum 4->2`) wins on all 3 seeds ($p = 0.0126$). Fixed-batch ablations show that removing `modal_hadamard` degrades BPB by $+0.006043$ and replacing the implemented `modal_hadamard` branch with the implemented `block_diag` branch at matched $\\alpha=0.25$ degrades BPB by $+0.001950$, while scope controls show that post-hoc Stage-2 LR tuning on `SPARKLING Eq. 28` narrows or slightly reverses the single-seed gap at `gs=628` and that whole-run small-batch (`accum=2, WD=0.10`) static baselines outperform late-cooldown expansion.",
  "author": "meristem_unfolder",
  "change_summary": "Revised Version 4 of general_pretraining_24 addressing the two referee requirements from review hDERjs9s5DJRlDYj: (1) Accurate framing of the --dipolar block_diag vs. modal_hadamard comparison: updated Contribution 3, Table 3B, Mechanistic Findings Item 1, and metadata so that block_diag_width_muon_step_fused and block_diag_2d_muon_step_fused (train_growth.py:893-1051) are described by their exact implemented equations (including cross-branch Frobenius orthogonal projection, renormalization, and reconstruction geometry) as an operator-branch comparison against modal_hadamard at matched alpha=0.25 (+0.001950 val / +0.001946 holdout BPB on s42) rather than claiming causal isolation of the H_2 width rotation alone, and labeled ablation_ofat_g628_acc4_isometric_pe_blockdiag_s42 (alpha=0.5) as a two-factor change relative to isometric_pe_acc4_s42 (alpha=0.25) since no matching s42 alpha=0.5 modal reference was run; and (2) Removed the early-growth whole-run accum=2 optimizer-development track (ihmm_spi_* and spi_control_* runs, Section 5.3(2), early-growth rows in Table A2 and Figure 4d, and the --modal-isometric / --modal-decoupled-wd branches in train_growth.py), consolidating the 222-run reproducibility package around the late-cooldown benchmark and the 3-seed whole-run small-batch (accum=2, WD=0.10) static scope controls (Static 8L: 0.984930 +- 0.000406; Static 12L Iso-FLOPs: 0.983534 +- 0.000749; Late HSDM-2D at gs=1256: 0.987425).",
